<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="242c" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Demo BFF refresh — .NET 10 runtime, settings parity, start and /healthz 200 (found by T242b)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — follow-on of plan §7 T242 (filed 2026-10-04, owner: "file a demo-refresh task")</phase>
    <gate>T242b merged to master (a master build is T242+); every live step needs owner confirmation</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Live configuration of an App Service in its own subscription; the setting values decide which resources the demo BFF talks to.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Judgment per missing setting (which demo resource, whether it exists, whether the feature should be off) and an owner decision on rebuilding demo as a stamp.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>live operations in the demo subscription</parallel-reason>
    <tags>deploy, azure, bff-api, demo, model1-dedicated</tags>
    <deps>242b</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Bring the demo BFF `spaarke-bff-demo` up to the current build's requirements so it starts and serves /healthz 200,
    then leave it in the run state the owner chooses — each live step confirmed with the owner first.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform operator-developer (Azure App Service, BFF configuration). Follow the live-action rules strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    `spaarke-bff-demo` runs on the `DOTNETCORE|10.0` stack with every setting the current BFF requires at startup (or the
    owning feature explicitly disabled), a current master build deployed, /healthz 200, Redis on `spaarke-bff-redis-demo`
    (managed identity, already set by T242b), and the run state the owner picks.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-10-04 by T242b step 5 (owner chose "start demo"): `spaarke-bff-demo` (subscription "Spaarke Demo
      Environment" 2ff9ee48-6f1d-4664-865c-f11868dd1b50, rg-spaarke-demo, westus2, UAMI `mi-bff-api-demo` client
      b0ce4ca4-…, `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production`) had been Stopped. The T242 build deployed (hashes verified) but the
      container could not launch: linuxFxVersion `DOTNETCORE|8.0`, only .NET 8.0.31 installed, the BFF targets .NET 10
      (dotnet-10-upgrade-r1). Demo also carries 157 settings vs dev's 206; 81 dev settings are absent (by prefix: AiSearch
      10, Communication 7, Membership 7, Ciam 7, Logging 5, Compose 3, RecordSync 3, PublicConfig 3, AiSafety 3, and one
      each of AzureAd, AzureOpenAI, DocumentIntelligence, ServiceBus, SharePointEmbedded, EmailProcessing,
      ExternalAccess, Features, APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING, …). The app was stopped again; Redis is done
      (`spaarke-bff-redis-demo`, `Redis__Enabled=true`, `Redis__Endpoint`, no connection string — T242b).
      Demo is not a provisioned stamp (no customer.bicep deployment); whether to keep hand-maintaining it or rebuild it
      as a stamp through L2 is an owner decision this task surfaces, not one it makes.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 (`-Environment demo` accepted since T242b; demo is in its own subscription — run with AZURE_CONFIG_DIR on a private copy of the az config, never `az account set`)</file>
      <file>config/environments.json (`demo` entry, requiredCorsOrigins empty)</file>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml (per_env_settings = the settings a stamp BFF needs)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/*Module.cs (which settings each module validates on start)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/tasks/242b-dev-redis-managed-recreate.poml (notes)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="live-action rule (owner)">Ask the owner before each live step (runtime change, each settings batch, deploy, start/stop). Never create, seed or restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either casing) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret`; never delete Key Vault secrets.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Only `spaarke-bff-demo` and its settings in rg-spaarke-demo. Create no new Azure resource without a separate owner OK; a setting that needs a resource demo does not have is an escalation, not a guess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no placeholders">Never set a placeholder or a dev resource's value on demo. A feature whose resource is absent is turned off through its own Enabled flag (ADR-032 null objects) or escalated.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A required setting points at a resource that does not exist in the demo subscription → STOP and list the options (create it, disable the feature, or rebuild demo as a stamp).</trigger>
    <trigger>The gap is large enough that rebuilding demo as a provisioned stamp is the cheaper path → STOP and put that choice to the owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Read-only: list every setting the current BFF requires at startup (ValidateOnStart options + throwing module guards) and diff against demo's settings; for each missing one record the demo resource it needs and whether that resource exists. Present the table and a recommendation (hand-maintain vs. rebuild as stamp) to the owner.</step>
    <step order="2">Owner OK → set linuxFxVersion `DOTNETCORE|10.0`.</step>
    <step order="3">Owner OK → apply the agreed settings in one batch (one restart).</step>
    <step order="4">Owner OK → deploy the current master BFF build (`Deploy-BffApi.ps1 -Environment demo -ResourceGroupName rg-spaarke-demo -AppServiceName spaarke-bff-demo`), start, /healthz 200, log shows "Redis authentication is managed identity".</step>
    <step order="5">Leave the app in the owner's chosen run state; record every live change in current-task.md; close POML notes, TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="live">demo BFF on .NET 10 with complete settings, healthy, in the owner's chosen run state</output>
    <output type="file-modified">this POML notes, TASK-INDEX, current-task live-changes log</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`spaarke-bff-demo` linuxFxVersion is `DOTNETCORE|10.0`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the app started, /healthz returns 200 and the log shows "Redis authentication is managed identity".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No setting on demo holds a placeholder or another environment's resource value; every disabled feature is disabled through its Enabled flag and listed in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The app's final run state is the one the owner chose; every live step and its approval is logged in current-task.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Filed 2026-10-04 (session 36) from T242b step 5 at the owner's request ("Stop it; file a demo-refresh task"). Not a prerequisite of T186. OWNER DECISION 2026-10-05 (D27): demo is the next environment used to test the provisioning orchestration — this answers the escalation question above (rebuild through L2 rather than hand-maintain). Re-scope before executing: provision demo with the orchestration instead of hand-refreshing spaarke-bff-demo; confirm the scope with the owner first. Facts read 2026-10-05: rg-spaarke-demo has no AI Search service (spaarke-search-demo absent); spaarke-bff-demo has no deployment slot; config/environments.json + spaarke-resources.yaml corrected. ADDED BY T246 (2026-10-06): spaarke-bff-demo has NO AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint setting (read 2026-10-06), and since T246 the BFF refuses to start outside Development/Testing without it — whatever demo path is chosen must set it (a stamp provisioned through L2 gets it from customer.bicep + H4b; a hand-refresh must point it at a Content Safety account demo can reach with its managed identity, which needs Cognitive Services User there).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>FULL rigor; prescriptive steps; owner confirmation before every live step.</protocol>
  </execution>
  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-09">Step 1 done (read-only; master BFF booted locally as Production against demo's 157 settings).
    Demo app: Stopped, DOTNETCORE|8.0, B1, no slots; all 38 KV references Resolved. Startup blockers: runtime 10.0;
    APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING (demo has only the retired ApplicationInsights__ConnectionString);
    AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint — NO Content Safety account exists in the demo subscription (new resource);
    PublicConfig__BffUrl / MsalClientId (da03fe1a…) / TenantId. Degraded even after: no AI Search (spaarke-search-demo
    missing), no FIC on the demo app reg, no membership topic, no Compose/Email webhook secrets, ~40 settings master no
    longer reads (incl. plaintext BuilderAdmin__ApiKey, Email__WebhookSecret, Rag__ApiKey, PowerBi__ClientSecret).
    Recommendation (D27): rebuild demo as a provisioned stamp rather than hand-refresh; the hand-refresh needs a new
    Content Safety resource (POML escalation). Open: the fate of the unmanaged spaarke-demo Dataverse environment.
    Exact hand-refresh commands kept in the session report should the owner choose it. Owner decision pending.</note>
  </notes>
</task>
